2026-09-27T09:59:20.1720109Z Description:
2026-09-27T09:59:20.1720608Z This PPA contains more recent Python versions packaged for Ubuntu.
2026-09-27T09:59:20.1721099Z 
2026-09-27T09:59:20.1722268Z Disclaimer: there's no guarantee of timely updates in case of security problems or other issues. If you want to use them in a security-or-otherwise-critical environment (say, on a production server), you do so at your own risk.
2026-09-27T09:59:20.1723617Z 
2026-09-27T09:59:20.1723751Z Update Note
2026-09-27T09:59:20.1724021Z ===========
2026-09-27T09:59:20.1724445Z Please use this repository instead of ppa:fkrull/deadsnakes.
2026-09-27T09:59:20.1724880Z 
2026-09-27T09:59:20.1725011Z Reporting Issues
2026-09-27T09:59:20.1725311Z ================
2026-09-27T09:59:20.1725496Z 
2026-09-27T09:59:20.1725709Z Issues can be reported in the master issue tracker at:
2026-09-27T09:59:20.1726260Z https://github.com/deadsnakes/issues/issues
2026-09-27T09:59:20.1726591Z 
2026-09-27T09:59:20.1726747Z Supported Ubuntu and Python Versions
2026-09-27T09:59:20.1727416Z ====================================
2026-09-27T09:59:20.1727685Z 
2026-09-27T09:59:20.1727879Z - Ubuntu 22.04 (jammy) Python3.7+ (NOT Python3.10)
2026-09-27T09:59:20.1728433Z - Ubuntu 24.04 (noble) Python3.7+ (NOT Python3.12)
2026-09-27T09:59:20.1728932Z - Ubuntu 26.04 (resolute) Python3.7+ (NOT Python3.14)
2026-09-27T09:59:20.1729946Z - Note: Python 3.10 (jammy), Python3.12 (noble), Python3.14 (resolute) are not provided by deadsnakes as upstream ubuntu provides those packages.
2026-09-27T09:59:20.1730905Z 
2026-09-27T09:59:20.1731082Z Why some packages aren't built:
2026-09-27T09:59:20.1731934Z - Note: for 22.04+, older python versions requre libssl<3 so they are not currently built
2026-09-27T09:59:20.1732849Z - If you need these, reach out to asottile to set up a private ppa
2026-09-27T09:59:20.1733341Z 
2026-09-27T09:59:20.1733857Z The packages may also work on other versions of Ubuntu or Debian, but that is not tested or supported.
2026-09-27T09:59:20.1734530Z 
2026-09-27T09:59:20.1734677Z Packages
2026-09-27T09:59:20.1734989Z ========
2026-09-27T09:59:20.1735169Z 
2026-09-27T09:59:20.1737659Z The packages provided here are loosely based on the debian upstream packages with some modifications to make them more usable as non-default pythons and on ubuntu.  As such, the packages follow debian's patterns and often do not include a full python distribution with just `apt install python#.#`.  Here is a list of packages that may be useful along with the default install:
2026-09-27T09:59:20.1739970Z 
2026-09-27T09:59:20.1740326Z - `python#.#-dev`: includes development headers for building C extensions
2026-09-27T09:59:20.1826682Z - `python#.#-venv`: provides the standard library `venv` module
2026-09-27T09:59:20.1828222Z - `python#.#-distutils`: provides the standard library `distutils` module
2026-09-27T09:59:20.1829232Z - `python#.#-lib2to3`: provides the `2to3-#.#` utility as well as the standard library `lib2to3` module
2026-09-27T09:59:20.1830232Z - `python#.#-gdbm`: provides the standard library `dbm.gnu` module
2026-09-27T09:59:20.1831035Z - `python#.#-tk`: provides the standard library `tkinter` module
2026-09-27T09:59:20.1831705Z 
2026-09-27T09:59:20.1831854Z Third-Party Python Modules
2026-09-27T09:59:20.1832210Z ==========================
2026-09-27T09:59:20.1832427Z 
2026-09-27T09:59:20.1834042Z Python modules in the official Ubuntu repositories are packaged to work with the Python interpreters from the official repositories. Accordingly, they generally won't work with the Python interpreters from this PPA. As an exception, pure-Python modules for Python 3 will work, but any compiled extension modules won't.
2026-09-27T09:59:20.1835864Z 
2026-09-27T09:59:20.1836840Z To install 3rd-party Python modules, you should use the common Python packaging tools.  For an introduction into the Python packaging ecosystem and its tools, refer to the Python Packaging User Guide:
2026-09-27T09:59:20.1838493Z https://packaging.python.org/installing/
2026-09-27T09:59:20.1838823Z 
